From: "Barak A. Pearlmutter" <bap@debian.org>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 23:55:00 +0100
Subject: do not put the process id in ml-build's temporary file names

ml-build generates a small SML file whose name contains the process id,
and compiles it; the name is recorded in the resulting heap image, so
every run produces a different image.  Name the temporary files after
the heap file being built instead.

Forwarded: no
---
 config/_ml-build | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/config/_ml-build b/config/_ml-build
index 7146bcb..5bd41e6 100644
--- a/config/_ml-build
+++ b/config/_ml-build
@@ -93,6 +93,16 @@ else
     usage no CM description file specified
 fi
 
+# The name of the generated SML file below is recorded in the heap image
+# that we are about to build, so base the temporary file names on the heap
+# file rather than on the process id; otherwise the image depends on the
+# pid of this script.
+xx=`basename "$heap"`
+smlfile=$xx-export.sml
+cmfile=$xx-export.cm
+listfile=$xx-BOOTLIST
+linkargsfile=$xx-LINKARGS
+
 rare=XYZ_XXX_0123
 
 cat >$smlfile <<EOF
